cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use TGBS in your research, please cite the software using the
  metadata below. For reproducibility, consider citing the DOI of the
  specific TGBS release used in your work.

title: "Task Group Bandwidth Server (TGBS)"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Kooshmanian"
    given-names: "Merlin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7771-3585"

abstract: >
  Task Group Bandwidth Server (TGBS) is a Linux kernel scheduler extension
  providing temporal isolation for CPU cgroups through hierarchical
  deadline-server scheduling. TGBS allows workloads using different native
  Linux scheduling classes to coexist within the same bandwidth-isolated
  task group.

repository-code: "https://github.com/mkooshmanian/TGBS"
url: "https://github.com/mkooshmanian/TGBS"

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22108568"

license: "GPL-2.0-only"

keywords:
  - Linux kernel
  - scheduling
  - real-time systems
  - temporal isolation
  - hierarchical scheduling
  - CPU cgroups
  - containers
  - SCHED_DEADLINE